.TH "GDAL-RASTER-READ" "1" "Aug 18, 2026" "" "GDAL"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
gdal-raster-read \- Read a raster dataset (pipeline only)
.sp
Added in version 3.11.

.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
The \fBread\fP operation is for use in a \fI\%gdal pipeline\fP only, and reads a single input
raster dataset. This is the first step of a pipeline.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
* read [OPTIONS] <INPUT>
\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-

Read a raster dataset.

Positional arguments:
  \-i, \-\-input <INPUT>                  Input raster datasets [required]

Advanced Options:
  \-\-if, \-\-input\-format <INPUT\-FORMAT>  Input formats [may be repeated]
  \-\-oo, \-\-open\-option <KEY>=<VALUE>    Open options [may be repeated]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH STANDARD OPTIONS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-if, \-\-input\-format <format>
Format/driver name to be attempted to open the input file(s). It is generally
not necessary to specify it, but it can be used to skip automatic driver
detection, when it fails to select the appropriate driver.
This option can be repeated several times to specify several candidate drivers.
Note that it does not force those drivers to open the dataset. In particular,
some drivers have requirements on file extensions.
.sp
May be repeated.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-oo, \-\-open\-option <NAME>=<VALUE>
Dataset open option (format specific).
.sp
May be repeated.
.UNINDENT
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.SS Example 1: Read a GeoTIFF file
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ gdal raster pipeline read input.tif ! ... [other commands here] ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
Even Rouault <even.rouault@spatialys.com>
